// RUNTIME_ABORT_EXPECTED
// EXPECT-RUNTIME: String index out of bounds
// FDN-004 (D17, ROADMAP_v2.0.0.md): `s[i]` on a `string` is now bounds-
// checked at runtime -- before this, `"abc"[5]` compiled and silently read
// past the terminator, returning garbage (audit finding F-17). Unlike a
// fixed-size Turf array, ValueRangePass has no compile-time constant-
// folding path for a string index at all (markNode(), src/analysis/ValueRange.cpp,
// only ever looks at `S->Type->isArray()`), so even this literal,
// obviously-out-of-range index reaches the unconditional runtime
// `strlen()`-based check every string read gets (EmitStringBoundsCheck(),
// src/codegen/CodegenArray.cpp) rather than a compile-time diagnostic.
fn main(): int {
    immut s: string = "abc";
    immut c: char = s[5];
    return c to int;
}
